11:T1061,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get a free eye test at Specsavers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You qualify for a free NHS-funded eye test if you are under 16 (or under 19 in full-time education), aged 60 or over, receiving certain means-tested benefits such as Income Support or Pension Credit, diagnosed with diabetes or glaucoma, or if you are over 40 and have a close family member with glaucoma. Simply let the receptionist know your eligibility when booking, and bring proof to your appointment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the Specsavers two-for-one deal include?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Specsavers' two-for-one offer lets you choose two pairs of glasses from selected ranges for the price of one pair, starting from £25. Many customers use this to get a pair of prescription glasses and a pair of prescription sunglasses, or to choose different frames for work and leisure. The offer applies to frame and lens combinations from the designated two-for-one range, and additional lens upgrades such as anti-reflection coatings may cost extra."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Specsavers come to my home for an eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, Specsavers operates a domiciliary (home visit) eye test service for patients who are unable to leave home unaccompanied due to a physical or mental health condition or disability. A Specsavers optometrist will visit you at home with portable testing equipment and a selection of frames. If you qualify for an NHS eye test, the home visit is also free. To arrange a home visit, contact your local Specsavers store directly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should I have an eye test at Specsavers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Specsavers recommends that most adults have an eye test every two years, or more frequently if advised by their optometrist. Children, people with diabetes, those over 70, and anyone with a family history of eye disease should typically have their eyes tested annually. Regular eye tests are important not just for updating your prescription but for detecting eye conditions early, when they are most treatable."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Specsavers offer laser eye surgery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, Specsavers does not offer laser eye surgery or any surgical eye procedures. They are an optical retailer focused on eye testing, glasses, contact lenses, and hearing care. If you are interested in laser eye surgery, your Specsavers optometrist can advise you and refer you to an appropriate specialist or clinic."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I book a Specsavers appointment through eyetest.co.uk?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Specsavers is not currently available for booking through eyetest.co.uk. We list Specsavers as a reference so customers can compare services and prices across different opticians. To book directly, visit specsavers.co.uk or call your local Specsavers store. We are working to bring Specsavers availability to our platform in the future."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What hearing aid brands does Specsavers offer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Specsavers works with major hearing aid manufacturers and also offers its own Advance range of digital hearing aids. NHS hearing aids are available free of charge for eligible patients through Specsavers audiology clinics. Private hearing aids start from around £495 per ear. All hearing aids come with an aftercare package including follow-up appointments and adjustments."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to get glasses from Specsavers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Standard glasses orders from Specsavers typically take 7 to 10 working days to be ready for collection. More complex prescriptions, including varifocals and high-index lenses, may take a little longer. Specsavers will contact you by text message when your glasses are ready to pick up from the store. Some stores offer an express service for simple single-vision prescriptions, but availability varies."}}]}5:[["$","$L10",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Specsavers Optical Group\",\"url\":\"https://www.specsavers.co.uk\",\"description\":\"Specsavers is the UK's largest optical retailer, founded in Guernsey by Doug and Dame Mary Perkins. Known for their value-for-money approach and iconic advertising campaigns, they operate a joint-venture partnership model where each store is co-owned by local optometrists. They provide comprehensive eye care, hearing services, and home visit testing across the UK and internationally.\",\"foundingDate\":\"1984\",\"areaServed\":{\"@type\":\"Country\",\"name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"numberOfEmployees\":{\"@type\":\"QuantitativeValue\",\"name\":\"UK stores\",\"value\":900},\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.specsavers.co.uk\"],\"parentOrganization\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"eyetest.co.uk\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"}}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Opticians\",\"item\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/opticians\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Specsavers Optical Group\",\"item\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/opticians/specsavers\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$11"}}],"$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15",false,"$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d"]}],"$L1e"]
